Q: iTunes/Apple Music Persistent ID A: <p>Expanding on @matt answer.</p>
<p>As of 2026, in Swift, <code>iTunesLibrary</code> <code>ITLibMediaItem.persistentID</code> is an <code>uint64_t</code> wrapped inside <code>NSNumber</code>.</p>
<p>All of the following work (you only need one of them, result are same):</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>var item: ITLibMediaItem
// *MUST* specify unsigened integer (.uintValue)
var persistentID_1: String = String(format: &quot;%lX&quot;, item.persistentID.uintValue) }
var persistentID_2: String = String(item.persistentID.uintValue, radix: 16,uppercase: true) }
var persistentID_3: String = String(UInt(item.persistentID.uintValue), radix: 16, uppercase: true)
// More specific to 64 bit (.uint64Value)
var persistentID_4: String = String(format: &quot;%lX&quot;, item.persistentID.uint64Value) }
var persistentID_5: String = String(item.persistentID.uint64Value, radix: 16,uppercase: true) }
var persistentID_6: String = String(UInt(item.persistentID.uint64Value), radix: 16, uppercase: true)
</code></pre>
